{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791814142,"nonce":"HOxQiir4PLwma62MBg/G+a4oIlU=","title":"Omitted optional arguments shift later defaults into the wrong slots","message":"TestUnicode.testIO crashes in haxe_string_length during pathBoth(callback). The method declares callback:String-\u003eVoid, ?path:String, ?skipNonExistent:Bool = true. Its MIR passes the boxed Bool default in the String slot and leaves the Bool slot null. fill_default_args skips None entries in function_param_defaults instead of emitting a null slot, so any later default moves left. LLVM and Cranelift receive the wrong argument order.\n\nEvidence: unicode-io-v61-lldb3.log, unicode-io-v61-markers.log, and OptionalArgumentSlots.hx. The full v61 reports on Mac and NUC both score 1083/1092; this crash is reached by manually staging the upstream Unicode assets and invoking testIO in an isolated probe.","files":null}]}